Interpretation
  The old 1.95 target was a non-resonant convenience, not the theorem.
  HYP-2653c asks for C(k)=O(number of scale clusters), then a finite
  base span roughly C(k)/(cap_9-Q(8)).  For k=9, the observed resonant
  values still point to a bounded-span extension, not to a failure.

